1
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:47,839
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:55,305
2017 PRAGUE

3
00:00:57,265 --> 00:01:00,727
Right now, we are here at the Prague
Harmonie International Competition

4
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:01,644
finals venue.

5
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:04,856
Tonight marks the final round of the
competition and features the two

6
00:01:04,939 --> 00:01:05,774
finalists.

7
00:01:05,857 --> 00:01:09,527
Given the outstanding performances
they both delivered in the semifinals,

8
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:12,238
our attention is focused on tonight's
event.

9
00:01:38,973 --> 00:01:40,642
Let go! Outta my way!

10
00:03:04,809 --> 00:03:06,144
Where are we going now?

11
00:03:07,937 --> 00:03:10,356
Excuse me! Stop, stop, stop!

12
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,233
I want to go to the toilet!

13
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:15,195
What's wrong with YOU!

14
00:03:15,278 --> 00:03:17,071
I said I want to go to the toilet!

15
00:03:18,448 --> 00:03:19,407
Don't try anything.

16
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:22,160
Or I'll put a bullet
right between your eyes.

17
00:03:54,400 --> 00:03:55,360
What the hell, man?

18
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:56,361
Settle down!

19
00:03:56,444 --> 00:03:58,363
Try not to get blood all over the car.

20
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:01,908
You think you're better than me,
trying to tell me what to do,

21
00:04:01,991 --> 00:04:02,992
is that it??

22
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:13,920
Ah!

23
00:04:18,591 --> 00:04:19,425
Come here!

24
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:07,658
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

25
00:06:07,742 --> 00:06:11,496
We will now present a certificate of
commendation to Kang Pi-o for his role

26
00:06:11,579 --> 00:06:15,249
in elevating the prestige of Korea Arts
High School.

27
00:06:16,334 --> 00:06:19,295
Kang Pi-o, if you would,
please come up to the stage.

28
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:21,672
EPISODE 1

29
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:26,052
Dude. All this is kinda overkill.

30
00:06:26,135 --> 00:06:27,220
You were better.

31
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:44,112
This certificate is hereby awarded to
this student for elevating the prestige

32
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:47,865
of this school by winning the Grand
Prize at the twenty-seventh Lake Erie

33
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:50,159
International Junior Competition.

34
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,376
YEAR 1, CLASS 8 NAME: KANG PI-O

35
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:01,337
OCTOBER 17, 2016 KIM U-HYEOK
PRINCIPAL OF KOREA ARTS HIGH

36
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:06,509
NO MORE SPECIAL TREATMENT
FOR KANG SEUNG-WOON'S GRANDSON

37
00:07:06,592 --> 00:07:07,427
DROP OUT
GET LOST BASTARD GO AWAY BASTARD

38
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:08,719
Hey, Han-rim! Found him!

39
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:11,681
Ew…

40
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:15,226
Hey. Did you throw this in the trash?

41
00:07:16,978 --> 00:07:18,729
You are an obnoxious little shit.

42
00:07:19,856 --> 00:07:23,067
To think the entire school gathered
to put on a show for you just cos

43
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,902
you won first place at the competition…

44
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,946
That's a pretty messed up thing to do.

45
00:07:30,658 --> 00:07:33,411
Hey, are we all just extras to you?

46
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:37,039
Then again, winning a competition

47
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:41,252
must be a walk in the park for Kang
Seung-woon's grandson.

48
00:07:42,962 --> 00:07:44,213
Oh, you're laughing?

49
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:45,339
What's so funny?

50
00:07:49,010 --> 00:07:49,886
Hold on…

51
00:07:49,969 --> 00:07:52,680
you really think I'm the reason
you didn't win?

52
00:07:52,763 --> 00:07:54,682
If you're so bitter about not winning,

53
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:58,227
you should go practice some more
instead of picking fights.

54
00:07:58,311 --> 00:07:59,520
And stop blaming others.

55
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:01,898
I swear…

56
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:05,485
What about you?

57
00:08:06,277 --> 00:08:08,488
You're just trying to prove yourself,
right?

58
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:11,365
Cos you got family issues you need to
work out?

59
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,119
- Hey!
- Crap.

60
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:17,288
What do you guys think you're doing?

61
00:08:18,080 --> 00:08:19,290
Ach, what does she want?

62
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:23,085
Hey. You picking a fight?

63
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:25,588
- Leave him alone.
- Hey.

64
00:08:25,671 --> 00:08:27,340
Chill the heck out, Jae-in.

65
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:30,009
And quit letting this cocky D-bag
use you.

66
00:08:32,678 --> 00:08:33,513
Let's go.

67
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:35,348
Hey, wait up.

68
00:08:40,269 --> 00:08:41,103
Oh!

69
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:43,689
Hey! Hey, Kang Pi-o!

70
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:47,151
How many times do I have to tell
you, huh?

71
00:08:47,235 --> 00:08:48,361
Try and be a little humble.

72
00:08:48,444 --> 00:08:49,946
It's not gonna kill ya.

73
00:08:50,655 --> 00:08:53,282
Everyone at school is already INSANELY
jealous of you.

74
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:55,326
Did you HAVE to toss the certificate?

75
00:08:55,409 --> 00:08:58,329
I mean, couldn't you have at least
thrown it away at home?

76
00:08:59,830 --> 00:09:03,125
Why should I consider other people's
feelings in everything I do?

77
00:09:03,209 --> 00:09:04,252
Wow.

78
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:06,796
Seriously, dude…

79
00:09:08,673 --> 00:09:09,674
You a sociopath?

80
00:09:12,426 --> 00:09:14,637
Why don't you just get to the point.

81
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,555
Me?

82
00:09:16,514 --> 00:09:17,390
There wasn't one.

83
00:09:17,932 --> 00:09:19,809
Really? Never mind then.

84
00:09:20,851 --> 00:09:22,603
Uh, actually I was thinking… um…

85
00:09:22,687 --> 00:09:23,521
Sorry.

86
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:26,857
- Find someone else.
- You don't even know what I was gonna say.

87
00:09:26,941 --> 00:09:28,442
You wanted me to be your accompanist.

88
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:30,403
Oh? How did you know?

89
00:09:32,697 --> 00:09:34,115
Hey, Kang Pi-o~~~~.

90
00:09:34,198 --> 00:09:36,492
Come on, just hear me out for a second,
okay?

91
00:09:39,537 --> 00:09:40,788
Kang Pi-o~~~

92
00:09:42,081 --> 00:09:44,542
You know I wouldn't ask you if I had a
choice.

93
00:09:45,042 --> 00:09:46,961
But none of the others are any good.

94
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:50,131
There is absolutely no way I can play
with them.

95
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:51,966
I don't have time.

96
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:54,302
Oh, Come on, it's not that much.
Just three--

97
00:09:55,261 --> 00:09:56,095
Wait, no, no.

98
00:09:57,388 --> 00:09:58,222
Two times?

99
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:02,643
Oh, Come on~~~
it'll barely take up any of your time.

100
00:10:02,727 --> 00:10:04,812
Hm? Hey!

101
00:10:04,895 --> 00:10:07,315
I'm literally begging, can't you
do it like just one time?

102
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:08,232
Huh?

103
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:15,323
Look, our skill levels are too different.

104
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:19,035
If we played together, you'd probably
sound worse than you actually are.

105
00:10:19,118 --> 00:10:22,038
- Is that something you really want to do?
- Wow.

106
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:25,082
Do you even realize how harsh you sound?

107
00:10:25,791 --> 00:10:27,001
But you're right.

108
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:30,963
Could you please… use your skills
to cover for me just this one time?

109
00:10:33,257 --> 00:10:34,091
No.

110
00:10:34,175 --> 00:10:35,009
- I won't.
- Hey!

111
00:10:35,092 --> 00:10:35,926
Kang Pi-o!

112
00:10:41,932 --> 00:10:43,851
Hello Genius, I'm talking to you!

113
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:16,884
Yeah.

114
00:11:18,052 --> 00:11:20,096
This is exactly the reason why…

115
00:11:20,596 --> 00:11:21,472
I can't lose you.

116
00:11:23,307 --> 00:11:26,143
How do you pull off Schumann so
beautifully like that?

117
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:45,955
Pfft…

118
00:11:47,623 --> 00:11:48,541
Kang Pi-o.

119
00:11:52,628 --> 00:11:53,838
Forget the accompaniment.

120
00:11:53,921 --> 00:11:54,880
You and me…

121
00:11:55,715 --> 00:11:57,091
We should just get married.

122
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:00,678
Seriously…

123
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:03,764
I never want to stop hearing you play.

124
00:12:10,187 --> 00:12:11,605
Would you just leave me alone?

125
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:14,066
No, I mean it - Let's get married!

126
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:17,153
SONGMIN HIGH SCHOOL

127
00:12:17,737 --> 00:12:19,655
Pass! Pass it! Hey!

128
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:36,380
SLIDE TO OPEN SLIDING DOOR

129
00:12:40,551 --> 00:12:41,552
Where are you going?

130
00:12:52,688 --> 00:12:54,398
- Watch it.
- Hey!

131
00:13:03,699 --> 00:13:05,576
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo, get up right now!

132
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:07,912
Gather 'round, guys.

133
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,915
Ugh…

134
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:13,334
We gotta talk.

135
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:15,669
Your music assessment's coming.

136
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:19,131
Do you all really not know how to play an
instrument?

137
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:20,966
- What assessment?
- Nah, we don't.

138
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,135
How many times do I have to tell you?

139
00:13:23,219 --> 00:13:26,055
At least use a triangle or something and
get it done.

140
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:31,393
Look if that's not gonna work…

141
00:13:32,603 --> 00:13:36,190
A friend of mine called and said they
need people to fill seats for this.

142
00:13:36,273 --> 00:13:38,692
If you go to this,
I'll count it as your assessment.

143
00:13:38,776 --> 00:13:41,362
- How's that?
- Oh, too bad, I don't feel like going.

144
00:13:41,987 --> 00:13:42,863
Why not, huh?

145
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:45,407
I'm trying real hard to make this easy
for you.

146
00:13:45,491 --> 00:13:47,117
Nobody watches this stuff…

147
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:49,870
You're making us super uncomfortable.

148
00:13:49,954 --> 00:13:52,039
Um… Why don't you just give up on us?

149
00:13:52,122 --> 00:13:53,165
Choi Jeong-yo!

150
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:54,083
Here!

151
00:13:57,962 --> 00:13:58,921
I don't wanna go.

152
00:13:59,004 --> 00:13:59,964
Nah.

153
00:14:06,762 --> 00:14:08,138
Hello, Joe Rider

154
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:09,056
Ha - Shit…

155
00:14:10,808 --> 00:14:12,476
Man, you're freakin' diligent.

156
00:14:12,560 --> 00:14:14,061
You ever miss a day of school?

157
00:14:15,437 --> 00:14:16,939
Ya get into any trouble today?

158
00:14:17,606 --> 00:14:20,067
Maybe I should do something bad and get
expelled.

159
00:14:20,693 --> 00:14:22,111
Like you'd have the guts to.

160
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:25,531
- Hop on.
- Okay, let's go~~~!

161
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:34,915
Get cash fast.

162
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:36,834
DO YOU NEED QUICK CASH?

163
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:42,339
When it comes to a man…

164
00:14:43,632 --> 00:14:46,468
He should never forget the hard
times he's gone through.

165
00:14:47,761 --> 00:14:48,596
You boys…

166
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,391
When you make it big and are
raking it in…

167
00:14:52,933 --> 00:14:53,976
don't forget about me.

168
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:55,311
- Thank you, sir.
- Sure.

169
00:14:56,896 --> 00:14:58,355
- Here.
- Thank you, sir!

170
00:14:58,439 --> 00:14:59,398
You punk…

171
00:14:59,899 --> 00:15:01,817
I put a little extra in there… 'kay?

172
00:15:01,901 --> 00:15:03,694
- Here. Work hard.
- Thank you, sir.

173
00:15:03,777 --> 00:15:05,696
- You can all succeed.
- Thank you.

174
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:09,033
Oh-ho… Jeong-yo…

175
00:15:11,076 --> 00:15:12,411
Eat up, yeah?

176
00:15:13,454 --> 00:15:14,580
You look a bit skinny.

177
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:16,624
Yeah, that's right.

178
00:15:17,124 --> 00:15:19,209
Tell your dad - to pay me back, 'kay?

179
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:22,880
I'm so dead broke right now, y' know?
I mean, we're eating jjajangmyeon

180
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,340
every day. Okay?

181
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:25,841
Jeez.

182
00:15:26,383 --> 00:15:28,052
Ugh… Hello, this is Happy Loan.

183
00:15:28,135 --> 00:15:28,969
Oh.

184
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:30,262
- Hey, I'm good man.
- Oh, ma'am!

185
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,222
- I mean, Miss!
- Just take it, dumbass.

186
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,682
- I'm giving it to you.
- Yeah.

187
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:34,600
Shit.

188
00:15:34,683 --> 00:15:35,684
- Oh, dear.
- Now eat.

189
00:15:45,527 --> 00:15:47,738
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
TRADITIONAL MARKET

190
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:56,997
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
MUSIC MALL

191
00:16:15,391 --> 00:16:16,225
Ugh…

192
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:28,529
I told you not to keep bringing me things
LIKE THAT!

193
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:31,490
If you keep doing it,

194
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:35,369
You just make it so hard for me
to hate you, kid.

195
00:16:40,791 --> 00:16:41,625
Hey.

196
00:16:42,793 --> 00:16:44,461
Do you feel sorry for me too?

197
00:16:45,754 --> 00:16:48,590
Is that why you keep bringing me this
stupid stuff?

198
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:52,011
I feel sorry for you…

199
00:16:54,179 --> 00:16:55,472
And sorry for myself.

200
00:16:57,516 --> 00:16:59,393
I feel sorry for you…

201
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,898
And for myself too~~~

202
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:22,249
GRAND PRIZE PIANO, CHOI JEONG-YO

203
00:17:49,735 --> 00:17:52,154
DEMAND FOR PAYMENT OF OVERDUE INTEREST

204
00:17:56,575 --> 00:17:59,078
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

205
00:18:06,543 --> 00:18:08,212
- Hello.
- You're here.

206
00:18:09,463 --> 00:18:10,506
Are you eating enough?

207
00:18:10,589 --> 00:18:11,423
Of course.

208
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:18,699
Whoo! It's been a while since I've seen
performance like that, that was

209
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:19,616
incredible!

210
00:19:20,951 --> 00:19:23,829
How the heck is Hyun-soo still such
a good player?

211
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:26,915
Most people run out of talent by
middle age and just move their fingers

212
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:28,500
mechanically, without feeling.

213
00:19:29,626 --> 00:19:33,172
And Maestro Kang obviously loved
Hyun-soo's performance, too.

214
00:19:33,672 --> 00:19:36,216
I mean, if he doesn't like a show,
that man won't even shake your

215
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:37,301
hand before leaving.

216
00:19:37,843 --> 00:19:41,096
If you ask me, a conductor shouldn't
wear his emotions on his sleeve

217
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,515
like that. It only intimidates people.

218
00:19:45,851 --> 00:19:46,685
Is that right?

219
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:48,478
I suppose so.

220
00:19:50,105 --> 00:19:52,191
Have you found an orchestra… for Pi-o?

221
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:53,358
Oh, yeah.

222
00:19:53,442 --> 00:19:56,820
We have meetings with Gyeongseong
Philharmonic and Seonghan Philharmonic

223
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:57,738
early next week.

224
00:19:58,655 --> 00:19:59,698
Don't worry.~~~~

225
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:03,076
Oh, Pi-o won't have any trouble
finding an orchestra.

226
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:06,705
While I am happy that you're getting on
Hyun-soo's good side…

227
00:20:07,247 --> 00:20:10,751
if you start neglecting my son cos of it,
I'll terminate our contract.

228
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:13,795
Oh, come on, don't say that.

229
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,255
There's no way I could.

230
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:18,842
The entire company is fully invested in
him right now.

231
00:20:21,637 --> 00:20:22,471
Hey,

232
00:20:22,554 --> 00:20:25,766
Jae-in told me you turned her down
when she asked for your help.

233
00:20:26,808 --> 00:20:27,643
I'm sorry.

234
00:20:29,144 --> 00:20:30,103
Nah, it's all right.

235
00:20:30,187 --> 00:20:32,397
It was the right call. To be honest,

236
00:20:32,481 --> 00:20:35,651
I'd rather you spent the time
practicing than accompanying her.

237
00:20:35,734 --> 00:20:37,152
It's more beneficial for me.

238
00:20:38,403 --> 00:20:40,989
Plus, I'm scared your mom will grab me by
the hair.

239
00:20:44,451 --> 00:20:45,911
… Really enjoyable. Honestly.

240
00:20:46,828 --> 00:20:49,248
Performing with you today made
me realize…

241
00:20:49,331 --> 00:20:50,874
What an absolute honor it is…

242
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:52,251
to share the stage with you.

243
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:53,961
Oh, not at all, sir. Thank you.

244
00:20:54,044 --> 00:20:55,045
Really.

245
00:20:58,674 --> 00:20:59,508
Oh, you're here.

246
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:06,640
You're late.

247
00:21:09,142 --> 00:21:09,977
Uh,

248
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:12,980
Mister Kang said he didn't want
to part ways just yet, so…

249
00:21:13,063 --> 00:21:14,022
I…

250
00:21:14,856 --> 00:21:16,108
enjoyed your performance.

251
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:17,985
Thanks a lot. Mm.

252
00:21:18,068 --> 00:21:20,279
I heard Hyun-jeong made you an offer.

253
00:21:20,362 --> 00:21:22,864
Yeah, I'll be staying in Korea for
the time being.

254
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:25,242
I guess you've eaten already.

255
00:21:25,325 --> 00:21:27,828
- Come in and have a drink with us.
- No, thank you.

256
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:33,208
So you're Pi-o, huh?

257
00:21:34,835 --> 00:21:35,669
Ah…

258
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:38,380
I've heard a lot about you.

259
00:21:38,463 --> 00:21:40,132
You won first place at Lake Erie?

260
00:21:41,425 --> 00:21:42,259
Wow.

261
00:21:42,968 --> 00:21:45,345
Well, as expected of your grandson.
It seems he inherited your

262
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:46,930
musical talent.

263
00:21:47,014 --> 00:21:48,890
Save your flattery for someone else.

264
00:21:49,891 --> 00:21:53,186
There's no need to give an untalented
kid false hope. Be selective with your

265
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:54,104
compliments.

266
00:21:54,771 --> 00:21:55,897
Speaking empty words…

267
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:58,650
is worse than saying nothing at all.

268
00:21:58,734 --> 00:22:00,569
- Father.
- Go upstairs.

269
00:22:01,611 --> 00:22:03,864
I don't want to ruin my good mood
tonight.

270
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:21,173
Hyun-soo was right there, how could you
say something so horrible?

271
00:22:21,256 --> 00:22:23,175
You can hate me all that you want.

272
00:22:23,258 --> 00:22:25,969
But did you have to talk like that in
front of the kid?

273
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:28,513
Just because you devoted your
life to your child, doesn't mean you can

274
00:22:28,597 --> 00:22:29,639
expect the same from me.

275
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:32,309
But you know he's your family too, he's
your grandson!

276
00:22:32,392 --> 00:22:34,603
- And he's my son!
- Don't get the wrong idea.

277
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:37,898
The only reason I let you two stay under
my roof…

278
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:40,650
is because I take pity on the way
you struggle so hard as a mother,

279
00:22:40,734 --> 00:22:42,903
not because I acknowledge him as my
grandson.

280
00:22:42,986 --> 00:22:44,696
Why can't you acknowledge him?

281
00:22:44,780 --> 00:22:45,614
Why?

282
00:22:45,697 --> 00:22:48,367
You expect me to accept him as my
grandson when I don't know who

283
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:49,284
his father is?

284
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:52,621
And above all, he doesn't have what it
takes.

285
00:22:53,455 --> 00:22:56,166
Stop wasting your time on that
half-witted boy, and focus on

286
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:57,626
getting your life together!

287
00:22:58,627 --> 00:22:59,461
Father!

288
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:07,928
Begin.

289
00:23:38,708 --> 00:23:41,586
Hail, Mary, full of grace, the lord
is with thee.

290
00:23:42,921 --> 00:23:48,343
Blessed art thou amongst women, and
blessed is the fruit of thy womb, Jesus.

291
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:51,555
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

292
00:23:52,764 --> 00:23:53,974
pray for us sinners,

293
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:57,269
now and at the hour of our death.

294
00:23:58,103 --> 00:23:58,937
Amen.

295
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:03,775
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

296
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:06,611
pray for us sinners

297
00:24:08,238 --> 00:24:10,282
now and at the hour of our death.

298
00:24:10,991 --> 00:24:11,825
Amen.

299
00:24:12,409 --> 00:24:13,743
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

300
00:24:15,579 --> 00:24:17,372
pray for us sinners

301
00:24:18,582 --> 00:24:20,917
now and at the hour of our death.

302
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:22,961
Amen.

303
00:24:25,881 --> 00:24:26,715
Come in.

304
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:42,272
I have something to tell you.

305
00:24:43,148 --> 00:24:44,274
Grandfather,

306
00:24:44,774 --> 00:24:47,152
do you really think I don't have what
it takes?

307
00:24:47,235 --> 00:24:51,114
Could it be that you only want to
believe that because you hate me so much?

308
00:24:52,365 --> 00:24:55,368
I have looked up to you since I was
a kid, do you know that?

309
00:24:55,994 --> 00:24:58,788
I practiced day and night because I
wanted to hear a single word of praise

310
00:24:58,872 --> 00:24:59,706
from you.

311
00:25:00,207 --> 00:25:02,584
But no matter how many times I won
first place,

312
00:25:03,210 --> 00:25:05,378
you never even bothered to look at me
once.

313
00:25:06,046 --> 00:25:07,839
If that's just because you hate me
so much--

314
00:25:07,923 --> 00:25:09,341
So what you're saying is…

315
00:25:14,095 --> 00:25:15,931
"Why would I belittle someone

316
00:25:16,014 --> 00:25:18,683
as talented as you because of my personal
feelings?"

317
00:25:20,977 --> 00:25:21,978
Is that it?

318
00:25:56,596 --> 00:25:58,181
What do you think you're doing?

319
00:26:02,394 --> 00:26:05,188
Do you think I care to see you show
off your technique?

320
00:26:56,531 --> 00:26:59,451
That's the best you can do, and you
have the nerve to say you're treated

321
00:26:59,534 --> 00:27:00,368
unfairly?

322
00:27:01,119 --> 00:27:04,623
Your amateur playing reeks of vanity and
has zero musical soul

323
00:27:07,917 --> 00:27:10,670
The people that I despise above all else
in this world…

324
00:27:11,171 --> 00:27:13,465
are those who think they themselves
are great

325
00:27:13,548 --> 00:27:16,551
just because they are able to play
challenging music.

326
00:27:17,260 --> 00:27:18,178
Unfortunately,

327
00:27:20,138 --> 00:27:21,139
you are one of them.

328
00:27:25,143 --> 00:27:27,270
I've never thought of myself that way!

329
00:27:27,354 --> 00:27:30,065
I only ever wanted your approval,
Grandfather. How is that such

330
00:27:30,148 --> 00:27:31,149
a bad thing, huh?

331
00:27:35,695 --> 00:27:36,529
One more chance.

332
00:27:37,572 --> 00:27:39,324
Please give me one more chance.

333
00:27:40,408 --> 00:27:43,036
If you still don't think I'm good enough
after that…

334
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:45,747
then I'll give up the piano for good.

335
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:47,666
I have no time to spare for you.

336
00:27:48,249 --> 00:27:50,085
What if I play the Noblesse Concert?

337
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,088
You dumb arrogant brat.

338
00:27:54,631 --> 00:27:57,592
Just cos you won a few competitions,
you think you could play in something

339
00:27:57,676 --> 00:27:58,593
like that?

340
00:28:01,805 --> 00:28:02,639
What if I could?

341
00:28:04,432 --> 00:28:05,934
Will you come watch me play?

342
00:28:06,726 --> 00:28:07,560
Deal.

343
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:10,980
If you think you can pull it off,
then you should try.

344
00:28:11,064 --> 00:28:14,025
But if my opinion remains unchanged
after your performance…

345
00:28:15,360 --> 00:28:18,113
you will have to take responsibility
for what you said.

346
00:28:25,954 --> 00:28:27,455
What kind of nonsense is this?

347
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:31,710
Why would you suddenly want to change
instructors?

348
00:28:32,293 --> 00:28:35,547
Don't you know how good it is to be
connected to Professor Seo?

349
00:28:35,630 --> 00:28:37,424
I don't really care who he's
connected to.

350
00:28:37,507 --> 00:28:38,717
I need a real instructor

351
00:28:40,635 --> 00:28:41,928
who can teach me properly.

352
00:28:42,011 --> 00:28:42,971
Oh, How can that…

353
00:28:45,432 --> 00:28:46,975
Connections are important.

354
00:28:47,058 --> 00:28:49,310
In the end, this industry is just a
business.

355
00:28:50,729 --> 00:28:51,563
Besides…

356
00:28:51,646 --> 00:28:53,857
of all people you want Hyun-soo,
is that it?

357
00:28:55,233 --> 00:28:56,693
No matter how talented he is,

358
00:28:57,318 --> 00:28:58,778
he's still just a performer.

359
00:28:59,571 --> 00:29:00,530
I told Grandfather

360
00:29:01,406 --> 00:29:04,409
that I would show him what I can do at
the Noblesse Concert.

361
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:06,745
If he doesn't approve of me then…

362
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:09,664
I'll quit playing the piano.
How will Professor Seo…

363
00:29:10,790 --> 00:29:12,208
teach me what I need?

364
00:29:12,292 --> 00:29:14,085
We haven't even talked about this.

365
00:29:14,753 --> 00:29:16,004
Why? Pi-o, you--

366
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:19,549
Off to school?

367
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:27,974
Have a good day.

368
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:34,314
Mm.

369
00:29:36,608 --> 00:29:38,067
You know, Pi-o's a smart kid.

370
00:29:38,985 --> 00:29:42,071
He knows exactly what he needs and takes
the steps to get it.

371
00:29:44,449 --> 00:29:47,619
You're standing on the sidelines,
what does this matter to you?

372
00:29:50,246 --> 00:29:51,831
Why are you being so prickly?

373
00:29:53,291 --> 00:29:54,125
Let's be frank.

374
00:29:54,793 --> 00:29:56,419
Everyone in the music world knows…

375
00:29:56,503 --> 00:29:58,379
Seo's reputation is overblown.

376
00:30:00,131 --> 00:30:00,965
I think…

377
00:30:01,049 --> 00:30:03,635
Pi-o made the right decision for what he
needs.

378
00:30:03,718 --> 00:30:07,305
If Father had just supported him, I would
never have thought of turning to

379
00:30:07,388 --> 00:30:08,223
Professor Seo.

380
00:30:09,682 --> 00:30:13,061
How would you know how it feels to be so
powerless, Mother dearest?

381
00:30:54,185 --> 00:30:55,019
Wow…

382
00:30:56,521 --> 00:30:58,064
You're a really good player.

383
00:30:58,690 --> 00:31:01,067
I mean, I don't see a single flaw
to point out.

384
00:31:01,693 --> 00:31:02,819
Why did you come here?

385
00:31:03,319 --> 00:31:05,280
I don't think you need my help at all.

386
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:06,698
You can tell the truth.

387
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:11,202
Be honest. You didn't like my playing did
you?

388
00:31:12,829 --> 00:31:13,997
No, quite the opposite.

389
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:15,707
Mm…

390
00:31:17,041 --> 00:31:20,169
Professor Seo… has done a fine job…
stick with him.

391
00:31:29,929 --> 00:31:31,055
Why? What did he say?

392
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:57,081
Professor Seo… has done a fine job… stick
with him.

393
00:31:59,208 --> 00:32:02,128
That's the best you can do, and you
have the nerve to say you're treated

394
00:32:02,211 --> 00:32:03,046
unfairly?

395
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:07,216
Your amateur playing reeks of vanity and
has zero musical soul

396
00:32:12,680 --> 00:32:15,683
ARTS & MUSIC HALL

397
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,085
Ugh, I'm so sleepy.

398
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:46,297
Man… I can't listen to this anymore.

399
00:32:47,507 --> 00:32:49,550
- Let's bounce.
- Sure. Okay.

400
00:32:49,634 --> 00:32:52,095
Ugh…
Let's go before Teach shows up, come on.

401
00:32:52,178 --> 00:32:53,012
Okay.

402
00:32:54,138 --> 00:32:55,056
- Hurry.
- Let's go…

403
00:33:11,781 --> 00:33:13,199
Come on, Jeong-yo, let's go.

404
00:33:14,575 --> 00:33:15,743
Nah, you guys go ahead.

405
00:33:46,816 --> 00:33:48,026
PIANO OPEN REPERTOIRE

406
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:49,986
KANG PI-O (17) KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

407
00:33:50,778 --> 00:33:51,612
"Kang Pi-o"?

408
00:33:55,324 --> 00:33:58,536
Hey, do you have an extra handkerchief?

409
00:34:00,621 --> 00:34:01,456
Thanks…

410
00:34:01,539 --> 00:34:02,874
So, what's your name then?

411
00:34:02,957 --> 00:34:04,000
Kang Pi-o.

412
00:34:33,529 --> 00:34:35,782
Pi-o, look over here just once, please!

413
00:34:38,367 --> 00:34:39,285
Take a picture with us!

414
00:34:39,368 --> 00:34:41,579
Ooh, they know how impressive you are.

415
00:34:41,662 --> 00:34:42,955
Oh, my, it's Kang Pi-o!

416
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:45,750
- Look!
- Why are you in such a bad mood?

417
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:48,086
Mister Kang Pi-o,

418
00:34:48,169 --> 00:34:49,253
the perfectionist.

419
00:34:50,546 --> 00:34:52,131
Come on, what was it this time?

420
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:54,050
The cadenza was a mess.

421
00:34:54,592 --> 00:34:56,636
THE PART OF A CONCERTO WHERE
NEAR THE END OF A MOVEMENT

422
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:58,221
It wasn't like I practiced it.

423
00:34:58,304 --> 00:35:00,765
AND THE SOLOIST SHOWCASES
MASTERFUL TECHNIQUE AND IMPROVISATION

424
00:35:00,848 --> 00:35:03,643
Well… I've realized recently…

425
00:35:04,519 --> 00:35:07,230
that trying to be too flashy during
the cadenza

426
00:35:07,313 --> 00:35:08,731
can be a bit tacky.

427
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:10,733
When you played it low key…

428
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:13,319
I think it was good… for the orchestra.

429
00:35:14,487 --> 00:35:17,740
It's not always right for the pianist to
just do their own thing.

430
00:35:23,621 --> 00:35:25,373
- Huh? Oh, oh, Pi-o!
- Pi-o!

431
00:35:25,456 --> 00:35:27,458
- Hello, ma'am.
- Get in, kids.

432
00:35:28,042 --> 00:35:30,002
Oh, I left my sheet music in the
green room.

433
00:35:30,086 --> 00:35:30,920
Go get it.

434
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:33,714
Huh?

435
00:35:34,632 --> 00:35:35,716
I'll go with you.

436
00:35:41,389 --> 00:35:43,558
You to skipped school to come here,
right?

437
00:35:43,641 --> 00:35:45,059
What'll your teacher say?

438
00:35:45,977 --> 00:35:47,562
Well, my future husband…

439
00:35:48,104 --> 00:35:50,481
you're military exemption is on the line.

440
00:35:50,982 --> 00:35:51,899
School can wait.

441
00:35:52,984 --> 00:35:53,818
Let go.

442
00:35:59,949 --> 00:36:00,783
Who's playing?

443
00:36:02,034 --> 00:36:03,286
They're really good.

444
00:36:06,455 --> 00:36:07,290
Huh?

445
00:36:09,750 --> 00:36:12,837
Damn it! Hey. Hey, Kang Pi-o.

446
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:15,923
Just… Go. See who it is.

447
00:36:16,674 --> 00:36:17,758
Hello, ma'am.

448
00:36:18,342 --> 00:36:19,677
Uh, I have a cold…

449
00:36:20,178 --> 00:36:27,143
KANG PI-O

450
00:36:46,537 --> 00:36:47,538
What are you doing?

451
00:36:47,622 --> 00:36:50,166
How can you look at someone else's
sheet music!?

452
00:36:50,791 --> 00:36:52,543
Oh, uh, sorry.

453
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:55,421
Uh, I didn't mean to look at it.

454
00:36:56,172 --> 00:36:57,006
Jeez…

455
00:36:57,506 --> 00:36:58,341
Uh, hey…

456
00:37:00,718 --> 00:37:02,511
Um… Do you remember me?

457
00:37:03,638 --> 00:37:04,597
Who are you?

458
00:37:05,723 --> 00:37:06,557
Oh…

459
00:37:07,391 --> 00:37:09,644
Never mind. Sorry.

460
00:37:10,144 --> 00:37:12,355
By the way, your cadenza sounded a bit
dry.

461
00:37:12,438 --> 00:37:13,731
Was that on purpose?

462
00:37:19,862 --> 00:37:20,696
Oh, it's just…

463
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:23,616
That was…

464
00:37:24,492 --> 00:37:25,826
just the impression I got.

465
00:37:30,915 --> 00:37:33,042
Well… you're entitled to your opinion.

466
00:37:33,125 --> 00:37:34,627
But if you know so much,

467
00:37:35,628 --> 00:37:38,381
Why don't you get up on stage and show us
what you got?

468
00:37:42,843 --> 00:37:43,678
Was that you?

469
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:45,429
On the piano just now??

470
00:37:46,889 --> 00:37:48,057
Whoa, awesome.

471
00:37:49,016 --> 00:37:51,894
Hey, you, uh… play really well.

472
00:37:52,895 --> 00:37:54,814
What's your school? Seonye?

473
00:37:54,897 --> 00:37:55,815
Deokmyeong?

474
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:58,609
Huh? Hey,

475
00:37:58,693 --> 00:38:00,820
Hold up! Wait!

476
00:38:02,571 --> 00:38:04,573
Oh? "Songmin"?

477
00:38:05,574 --> 00:38:06,951
That's not an arts school.

478
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:08,995
Wow.

479
00:38:09,745 --> 00:38:11,330
That makes it even more insane.

480
00:38:12,665 --> 00:38:14,750
Hold on… um,

481
00:38:14,834 --> 00:38:16,711
Can you give me your social or phone
number?

482
00:38:16,794 --> 00:38:18,087
Uh… Well, you see, I play the

483
00:38:18,170 --> 00:38:20,047
- viola, and--
- Oh, just leave me alone.

484
00:38:20,131 --> 00:38:21,716
- Jeez…
- Hey!

485
00:39:08,429 --> 00:39:10,848
By the way, your cadenza sounded a bit
dry.

486
00:39:10,931 --> 00:39:12,099
Was that purpose?

487
00:39:23,861 --> 00:39:27,698
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT STREET

488
00:39:53,265 --> 00:39:55,309
Hey, You gonna play?

489
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:57,228
Sorry, Ma'am, um…

490
00:39:58,062 --> 00:40:00,314
Instead of playing it without any
emotion…

491
00:40:02,024 --> 00:40:04,110
couldn't you put a little more heart into
it?

492
00:40:04,193 --> 00:40:05,528
I mean, It's like every note

493
00:40:05,611 --> 00:40:07,738
just sounds kinda flat, you know…?

494
00:40:07,822 --> 00:40:08,823
What are you saying?

495
00:40:09,365 --> 00:40:10,908
"You're" criticizing me?

496
00:40:10,991 --> 00:40:12,243
Yeah, I know.~~~

497
00:40:12,326 --> 00:40:13,828
I know I totally suck.

498
00:40:14,578 --> 00:40:17,081
That's why if you don't play well,
we're gonna be…

499
00:40:17,790 --> 00:40:19,041
so screwed~~~.

500
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:24,213
If you're so dissatisfied, go find
another accompanist.

501
00:40:25,798 --> 00:40:27,007
Huh? No wait, ma'am.

502
00:40:27,508 --> 00:40:29,009
That's not what I meant…

503
00:40:29,093 --> 00:40:30,094
Ma'am?

504
00:40:31,470 --> 00:40:32,304
Wait, Ma'am!

505
00:40:35,307 --> 00:40:36,142
Ugh…

506
00:40:47,319 --> 00:40:50,197
SONGMIN HIGH SCHOOL

507
00:40:52,867 --> 00:40:54,785
Whoa. She's pretty cute.

508
00:40:58,372 --> 00:40:59,206
Wow.

509
00:40:59,290 --> 00:41:01,000
- She's cute.
- She's really cute.

510
00:41:01,083 --> 00:41:02,042
What the?

511
00:41:03,669 --> 00:41:05,379
Shut up. Who are you?

512
00:41:05,463 --> 00:41:07,006
- Oh!
- Come on.

513
00:41:07,715 --> 00:41:08,841
Don't you remember me?

514
00:41:09,550 --> 00:41:11,677
The music hall? We met the other day?

515
00:41:13,429 --> 00:41:14,263
What the hell…

516
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:15,723
Listen…

517
00:41:15,806 --> 00:41:18,017
I totally fell in love with the way
you play.

518
00:41:18,100 --> 00:41:20,394
And I'm looking for an accompanist
right now.

519
00:41:21,020 --> 00:41:22,688
Could you please accompany me?

520
00:41:22,771 --> 00:41:24,732
- Get lost.
- Wait, what?

521
00:41:25,232 --> 00:41:26,692
You haven't heard me out.

522
00:41:27,526 --> 00:41:30,779
So, uh… I'll pay you a shed load of money.

523
00:41:31,822 --> 00:41:32,656
I said get lost.

524
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:35,117
Oh, okay, how about this then?

525
00:41:38,078 --> 00:41:39,121
Look, my mother…

526
00:41:39,788 --> 00:41:41,916
runs a classical artist management
agency.

527
00:41:43,083 --> 00:41:44,335
You accompany me…

528
00:41:44,418 --> 00:41:45,878
I'll get you an audition.

529
00:41:45,961 --> 00:41:47,838
From what I can tell, you're genius
level.

530
00:41:47,922 --> 00:41:50,841
Are you just going to let your talent go
to waste like this?

531
00:41:50,925 --> 00:41:52,384
What the hell are you talking about?

532
00:41:52,468 --> 00:41:56,305
You keep that "genius" crap to yourself.
This is some bullshit, I'm out.

533
00:41:59,225 --> 00:42:00,059
A million won!

534
00:42:07,983 --> 00:42:08,943
I don't believe it…

535
00:42:10,069 --> 00:42:11,779
Did you think I'd pay you peanuts?

536
00:42:12,655 --> 00:42:14,281
Of course you didn't.

537
00:42:15,324 --> 00:42:16,158
Normally,

538
00:42:16,700 --> 00:42:18,661
I pay 100,000 won per session,

539
00:42:19,745 --> 00:42:21,080
but you're special, right?

540
00:42:21,705 --> 00:42:24,291
Two hundred thou.
So, if you do five sessions with me…

541
00:42:24,375 --> 00:42:25,501
That's a…

542
00:42:27,253 --> 00:42:28,420
million. Wow!

543
00:42:29,338 --> 00:42:31,757
That sounds like a pretty sweet gig, am I
right?

544
00:42:32,967 --> 00:42:34,593
Oh, you're a cocky little shit.

545
00:42:36,345 --> 00:42:37,179
So?

546
00:42:38,430 --> 00:42:40,057
What's wrong with my teaching?

547
00:42:40,849 --> 00:42:42,184
What's the matter with it?

548
00:42:42,977 --> 00:42:45,854
You think I don't give a damn about
musicality, and I'm just running a

549
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:47,022
college prep factory?

550
00:42:48,023 --> 00:42:48,857
Just tell me, kid.

551
00:42:48,941 --> 00:42:49,942
Who is it?

552
00:42:50,025 --> 00:42:53,195
You want to switch professors, but you
feel too guilty to leave, so you're just

553
00:42:53,279 --> 00:42:54,905
looking for an excuse, is that it?

554
00:42:54,989 --> 00:42:56,365
No, It's not like that.

555
00:42:56,865 --> 00:42:57,783
Like hell it isn't.

556
00:42:57,866 --> 00:42:59,868
Don't you bullshit me. Huh?

557
00:43:00,744 --> 00:43:03,205
Don't give me… bullshit like that~~~!

558
00:43:05,874 --> 00:43:08,210
I always felt like something
wasn't right,

559
00:43:08,294 --> 00:43:12,172
but you always just told me to copy your
playing style, so that's what I did.

560
00:43:12,256 --> 00:43:14,508
All you've done is make me a carbon copy
of you.

561
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:15,426
What?

562
00:43:17,261 --> 00:43:18,095
I'm finished.

563
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:22,516
Get out. Don't show your face to me again.

564
00:43:23,601 --> 00:43:24,435
You…

565
00:43:24,518 --> 00:43:27,813
I'll do whatever it takes to make sure
you never get a foothold in

566
00:43:27,896 --> 00:43:29,815
this industry. Get out.

567
00:43:30,316 --> 00:43:31,150
Get out!

568
00:43:48,626 --> 00:43:49,793
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo.

569
00:43:50,336 --> 00:43:51,545
- Oh, hello.
- Let's go.

570
00:43:51,629 --> 00:43:53,297
- Hello, kids.
- Hello, ma'am.

571
00:43:53,380 --> 00:43:55,049
- Let's go home.
- It's heavy right?

572
00:43:55,132 --> 00:43:56,133
Oh!

573
00:44:04,850 --> 00:44:06,018
You practiced, right?

574
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:11,231
That one. Play it.

575
00:44:11,315 --> 00:44:12,232
Pay me first.

576
00:44:12,775 --> 00:44:14,735
Wow… So it's like that.

577
00:44:19,698 --> 00:44:20,532
Here.

578
00:44:21,492 --> 00:44:23,577
Half up front. The rest when we're done.

579
00:44:24,078 --> 00:44:24,912
Will that work?

580
00:44:29,166 --> 00:44:30,000
Let's play.

581
00:45:26,557 --> 00:45:27,933
I hope you have a safe trip back.

582
00:45:28,016 --> 00:45:30,519
- Thanks.
- And I hope you'll consider…

583
00:45:31,770 --> 00:45:32,604
my offer.

584
00:45:33,105 --> 00:45:34,273
An evaluator like you…

585
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:36,483
could really serve the school.

586
00:45:36,567 --> 00:45:37,735
Well, I'll consider it.

587
00:45:38,777 --> 00:45:40,696
I wonder what we'll get this year.

588
00:45:40,779 --> 00:45:43,115
Last year, we had a fair share
of violinists…

589
00:45:44,283 --> 00:45:45,117
What is it?

590
00:46:20,235 --> 00:46:21,069
Who are you?

591
00:46:22,654 --> 00:46:23,864
What school do you go to?

592
00:46:23,947 --> 00:46:24,948
Oh,

593
00:46:25,032 --> 00:46:26,450
he's from another school.

594
00:46:26,533 --> 00:46:28,786
I just brought him in here as my
accompanist.

595
00:46:30,245 --> 00:46:31,079
I see.

596
00:46:37,252 --> 00:46:38,086
Wait…

597
00:46:38,837 --> 00:46:40,214
Hey! Stop!

598
00:46:41,965 --> 00:46:44,343
Hey! Wait! Wait!

599
00:46:45,177 --> 00:46:46,011
Hey!

600
00:46:46,094 --> 00:46:48,514
Let go, man! I just came here to do a
quick gig!

601
00:46:51,725 --> 00:46:52,684
Pay me first.

602
00:46:53,227 --> 00:46:54,478
I'm owed a hundred grand.

603
00:46:58,690 --> 00:46:59,525
Here.

604
00:47:00,609 --> 00:47:02,444
Play what you were playing earlier.

605
00:47:18,252 --> 00:47:19,628
Now, try modulating it.

606
00:47:33,892 --> 00:47:35,394
Okay, let's try a variation.

607
00:48:18,979 --> 00:48:20,355
What's your name young man?

608
00:48:23,025 --> 00:48:23,859
Choi Jeong-yo.

609
00:48:25,652 --> 00:48:26,570
Tell me, Jeong-yo,

610
00:48:27,279 --> 00:48:29,323
where do you take your piano lessons?

611
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:31,325
- I don't take any.
- What?

612
00:48:31,825 --> 00:48:34,494
I just play the piano at home when
I'm bored, is all.

613
00:48:36,830 --> 00:48:37,664
Look, uh…

614
00:48:38,332 --> 00:48:40,584
How 'bout you enroll here and learn
properly?

615
00:48:47,424 --> 00:48:48,258
Oh…

616
00:48:49,092 --> 00:48:50,802
So that's what this was all about.

617
00:48:55,432 --> 00:48:57,768
Sorry to break it to you, but I'm
not brainless.

618
00:48:57,851 --> 00:48:59,102
What's that supposed to mean?

619
00:48:59,186 --> 00:49:02,314
You're just looking for another
student to milk for money. Well, I don't

620
00:49:02,397 --> 00:49:03,231
have any.

621
00:49:04,107 --> 00:49:04,942
I'm out.

622
00:49:06,401 --> 00:49:07,235
Actually, no.

623
00:49:08,403 --> 00:49:10,948
We're willing to provide full support,
even a place in the dorms,

624
00:49:11,031 --> 00:49:11,865
if you need it.

625
00:49:12,449 --> 00:49:14,952
We have a scholarship program for gifted
students.

626
00:49:15,494 --> 00:49:18,205
You wouldn't have to worry about
tuition or practice fees. All you'd

627
00:49:18,288 --> 00:49:19,247
have to do is play.

628
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:21,166
And then what'll I do?

629
00:49:22,167 --> 00:49:24,252
How'll I make a living playing the piano?

630
00:49:25,212 --> 00:49:27,005
It's easy for people like you, uh…

631
00:49:28,048 --> 00:49:29,299
You guys have money.

632
00:49:29,383 --> 00:49:31,510
You can afford to be artists, but for
me…?

633
00:49:32,052 --> 00:49:32,886
Man…

634
00:49:35,305 --> 00:49:37,015
I'd starve to death if I did that.

635
00:49:38,058 --> 00:49:38,892
Have a good one.

636
00:49:40,060 --> 00:49:40,894
Wait a minute.

637
00:49:42,813 --> 00:49:45,273
Call me… if you ever change your mind.

638
00:49:47,859 --> 00:49:49,486
Uh… Nah…

639
00:49:51,530 --> 00:49:52,656
From what I've seen…

640
00:49:53,448 --> 00:49:55,951
I don't think you'll need to worry about
starving.

641
00:49:56,952 --> 00:49:58,245
Call me when you're ready.

642
00:49:58,328 --> 00:50:00,247
All right? Hm?

643
00:50:01,081 --> 00:50:01,915
Sure.

644
00:50:03,500 --> 00:50:04,334
Goodbye.

645
00:50:19,766 --> 00:50:20,600
Woah!

646
00:50:21,226 --> 00:50:22,060
Hold on…

647
00:50:22,144 --> 00:50:24,521
Did Director Yoon just offer you a
scholarship?

648
00:50:25,856 --> 00:50:27,274
Wow, no way, no way!

649
00:50:28,358 --> 00:50:29,484
See, dummy~~~!?

650
00:50:29,568 --> 00:50:30,694
I told you ~~~!

651
00:50:30,777 --> 00:50:32,154
You're definitely a genius.

652
00:50:33,238 --> 00:50:35,949
I knew it.
I, like, literally called it, didn't I?

653
00:50:37,993 --> 00:50:40,412
So, what'll you do?
You'll transfer, right?

654
00:50:41,288 --> 00:50:42,122
- No.
- What?

655
00:50:42,205 --> 00:50:43,040
Are you crazy?

656
00:50:45,459 --> 00:50:49,212
You might not know this~~, but everyone's
dying to get into this place.

657
00:50:49,296 --> 00:50:52,299
Dude, get a grip and seriously
think about it, okay?

658
00:50:52,382 --> 00:50:54,259
Chances like this are rare you know.

659
00:50:54,760 --> 00:50:56,261
I said no.

660
00:50:56,887 --> 00:50:58,764
Huh? Well, why not?

661
00:50:58,847 --> 00:50:59,723
Give me a good reason.

662
00:50:59,806 --> 00:51:01,558
I don't know. I just don't want to.

663
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:03,852
Why do you care?

664
00:51:03,935 --> 00:51:04,811
You in cahoots?

665
00:51:11,818 --> 00:51:13,737
Who the heck was that kid?

666
00:51:15,363 --> 00:51:18,408
He's a bit rough around the edges,
but you can't deny it; he's got a

667
00:51:18,492 --> 00:51:20,452
real gift. Wow,

668
00:51:20,535 --> 00:51:23,371
I don't think I've heard anyone
play quite like that.

669
00:51:23,455 --> 00:51:24,706
Tell me something…

670
00:51:25,499 --> 00:51:27,709
what made you suggest that he
transfer here?

671
00:51:29,795 --> 00:51:30,962
Around seven years ago…

672
00:51:31,588 --> 00:51:34,216
I was judging a competition and heard
this kid play.

673
00:51:34,716 --> 00:51:37,719
And for some reason, his performance
just stuck with me.

674
00:51:37,803 --> 00:51:40,847
Ever since then, I've regretted
letting him slip away.

675
00:51:41,556 --> 00:51:42,516
That kid.

676
00:51:42,599 --> 00:51:44,017
You know what his name was?

677
00:51:44,643 --> 00:51:45,894
It was Choi Jeong-yo.

678
00:51:49,773 --> 00:51:51,733
Hey bro. Help me pick one of these.

679
00:51:52,901 --> 00:51:53,944
I can't decide, man!

680
00:51:54,027 --> 00:51:54,861
Woah, hold on!

681
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:57,531
Dude, look. I'm trying to pick
between the white ones, or the ones

682
00:51:57,614 --> 00:51:58,865
with a red stripe.

683
00:51:58,949 --> 00:52:00,700
I mean, the whites are cool, right?

684
00:52:06,123 --> 00:52:07,999
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL DIRECTOR
YOON SEON-JU

685
00:52:08,083 --> 00:52:10,335
How 'bout you enroll here and learn
properly?

686
00:52:10,418 --> 00:52:11,253
Look, uh…

687
00:52:26,476 --> 00:52:27,310
Huh?

688
00:52:38,238 --> 00:52:39,114
Is that you, Dad?

689
00:52:48,415 --> 00:52:49,749
Right. Search the place.

690
00:52:49,833 --> 00:52:52,043
- Is he here?
- No, he's not.

691
00:52:52,127 --> 00:52:53,545
Oh, damn it…

692
00:52:54,546 --> 00:52:56,756
Kid… where did your dad go?

693
00:52:57,299 --> 00:52:58,675
- I don't know.
- Don't know?

694
00:52:58,758 --> 00:52:59,593
You sure?

695
00:53:04,055 --> 00:53:05,765
- Huh?
- Sucks for you…

696
00:53:06,725 --> 00:53:07,559
Oh…

697
00:53:07,642 --> 00:53:09,144
Sorry… let me see.

698
00:53:09,644 --> 00:53:12,314
Hold on. Okay, calm down, I'll be gentle.
Lemme see.

699
00:53:13,231 --> 00:53:14,983
Yeah, this'll do - we can use this.

700
00:53:15,650 --> 00:53:16,484
Kid.

701
00:53:17,152 --> 00:53:17,986
Call your daddy.

702
00:53:18,528 --> 00:53:19,613
Get him to come here.

703
00:53:19,696 --> 00:53:20,739
Okay?

704
00:53:21,364 --> 00:53:22,199
That's it.

705
00:53:23,617 --> 00:53:24,784
Oh, Cheese and rice…

706
00:53:25,452 --> 00:53:26,453
Give me a cigarette.

707
00:53:30,874 --> 00:53:31,875
HYUN, OCTOBER 28, 2016

708
00:53:31,958 --> 00:53:34,169
Kim's on his way over to your place
right now, man.

709
00:53:34,252 --> 00:53:35,128
You need to bail.

710
00:53:38,590 --> 00:53:40,008
Hey. Use that phone!

711
00:53:40,091 --> 00:53:40,926
- Hey!
- Fuck!

712
00:53:41,009 --> 00:53:41,843
- Boss!
- Ack!

713
00:53:47,224 --> 00:53:48,058
Shit…

714
00:53:50,769 --> 00:53:51,603
Whoa, whoa…

715
00:54:02,697 --> 00:54:04,491
- Shit!
- STOP, KID!

716
00:54:06,701 --> 00:54:08,453
- Whoa,!
- Ah, fuck!

717
00:54:15,252 --> 00:54:17,087
Ah! Shucks…

718
00:54:18,838 --> 00:54:19,673
Stop already.

719
00:54:21,132 --> 00:54:21,967
Damn it!

720
00:54:22,592 --> 00:54:24,386
- Oh, man, I'm outta shape.
- Fuck…

721
00:54:25,136 --> 00:54:25,971
Hey you!

722
00:54:26,054 --> 00:54:27,514
- 'Kay…
- What're you doing?

723
00:54:27,597 --> 00:54:28,515
No don't!

724
00:54:29,057 --> 00:54:29,891
Dammit!

725
00:54:30,684 --> 00:54:31,935
- Come on, get him!
- Yeah!

726
00:54:32,686 --> 00:54:33,520
Hurry!

727
00:54:33,603 --> 00:54:34,437
- C'mon!
- Yeah!

728
00:54:34,521 --> 00:54:35,355
Huh?

729
00:55:49,888 --> 00:55:51,097
What are you doing here?

730
00:56:02,734 --> 00:56:04,611
Drink this and dry off before you go.

731
00:56:05,278 --> 00:56:06,529
You don't wanna get sick.

732
00:56:08,031 --> 00:56:08,865
Sir, please,

733
00:56:09,949 --> 00:56:11,910
Can you just give me a straight answer?

734
00:56:12,619 --> 00:56:13,703
What's wrong with me?

735
00:56:15,330 --> 00:56:17,665
Not knowing what's wrong is driving
me insane.

736
00:56:23,004 --> 00:56:24,672
Everyone just tells me I'm good.

737
00:56:26,716 --> 00:56:28,301
But I know that I'm not.

738
00:56:29,552 --> 00:56:32,639
I don't know if they're just dumb, or
they really can't tell.

739
00:56:33,681 --> 00:56:35,225
But YOU know, Mister Do.

740
00:56:36,518 --> 00:56:37,352
Don't you?

741
00:56:43,817 --> 00:56:44,651
I do.

742
00:56:46,319 --> 00:56:48,696
I think there's a problem with your
musicality.

743
00:56:49,948 --> 00:56:52,033
I think, what's wrong with your playing…

744
00:56:52,742 --> 00:56:54,119
is it lacks your own voice.

745
00:56:54,828 --> 00:56:56,913
Right now, your brilliant technique

746
00:56:57,872 --> 00:57:00,250
is cleverly masking the flaws hiding
behind it.

747
00:57:01,209 --> 00:57:03,461
But if you listen closely,
you'll hear it.

748
00:57:03,545 --> 00:57:05,797
You'll hear that your music is
not genuine.

749
00:57:07,966 --> 00:57:10,552
Your technical skill is some of
the best I have seen,

750
00:57:10,635 --> 00:57:12,846
but having perfect "technique" isn't
enough.

751
00:57:15,473 --> 00:57:18,309
You need to make the E- MOTIONS
beyond the sheet music your own.

752
00:57:18,393 --> 00:57:20,228
Your pain, your joy, your despair.

753
00:57:21,146 --> 00:57:22,147
Your emotions…

754
00:57:23,148 --> 00:57:25,233
must hit the audience right in the heart.

755
00:57:30,613 --> 00:57:32,782
Otherwise, you'll never be a true
musician.

756
00:58:05,273 --> 00:58:06,816
I'd like a room, please.

757
00:58:07,358 --> 00:58:09,861
- We don't rent to minors.
- Uh, why not?

758
00:58:09,944 --> 00:58:11,863
Uh… Please ma'am, I have money.

759
00:58:12,864 --> 00:58:13,907
Just for the night.

760
00:58:15,783 --> 00:58:16,618
Go.

761
00:58:50,568 --> 00:58:51,402
Hello?

762
00:58:52,111 --> 00:58:52,946
Hello…

763
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:54,614
This is Choi Jeong-yo.

764
00:58:57,492 --> 00:58:58,952
I was wondering if I could…

765
00:59:00,995 --> 00:59:02,664
stay at the dorms for a few days?

766
00:59:32,151 --> 00:59:32,986
Look.

767
00:59:33,486 --> 00:59:36,447
Given your situation, why don't
you transfer to our school?

768
00:59:38,157 --> 00:59:41,327
This isn't out of pity or charity,
so don't get the wrong idea.

769
00:59:44,038 --> 00:59:44,872
Honestly,

770
00:59:44,956 --> 00:59:48,918
recruiting smart, talented students to
the school - looks really good for my

771
00:59:49,002 --> 00:59:49,836
record.

772
00:59:50,670 --> 00:59:52,297
And you fit the bill perfectly.

773
01:00:17,071 --> 01:00:20,325
The phone is turned off. After the
beep, you will be connected to

774
01:00:20,408 --> 01:00:22,410
voicemail, and call charges will apply.

775
01:00:22,910 --> 01:00:24,078
VOICE CALLING DAD

776
01:00:45,725 --> 01:00:47,560
CHOI JEONG-YO KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

777
01:01:01,532 --> 01:01:02,367
Listen up!

778
01:01:03,368 --> 01:01:05,536
We have a new transfer student in class.

779
01:01:05,620 --> 01:01:07,497
Make sure to take good care of him.

780
01:01:07,580 --> 01:01:08,581
Introduce yourself.

781
01:01:16,506 --> 01:01:17,340
Hi, kids.

782
01:01:18,091 --> 01:01:18,925
Hello, ma'am.

783
01:01:19,676 --> 01:01:20,510
Oh.

784
01:01:26,557 --> 01:01:28,101
I haven't seen you before.

785
01:01:28,184 --> 01:01:30,978
- He's a transfer student.
- He's a transfer student.

786
01:01:31,062 --> 01:01:33,856
- What's your name?
- Choi Jeong-yo, ma'am.

787
01:01:35,233 --> 01:01:36,150
What's your major?

788
01:01:38,486 --> 01:01:40,154
- Piano.
- Hey, hey, hey.

789
01:01:40,238 --> 01:01:41,072
Oh.

790
01:01:41,155 --> 01:01:42,281
- Same major as you.
- A transfer? - I bet he's good.

791
01:01:42,365 --> 01:01:43,199
Oh, really?

792
01:01:43,783 --> 01:01:44,659
Come on up here.

793
01:01:45,159 --> 01:01:47,328
- She's gonna make him play.
- I know, right?

794
01:01:51,749 --> 01:01:52,583
Ooh…

795
01:01:58,923 --> 01:01:59,841
Play something.

796
01:02:04,262 --> 01:02:06,347
Well? Go on then.

797
01:02:10,184 --> 01:02:11,352
Oh, he's going to play.

798
01:02:11,853 --> 01:02:12,687
Cool

799
01:02:41,048 --> 01:02:41,883
Um…

800
01:02:43,634 --> 01:02:44,886
May I do it another time?

801
01:02:45,678 --> 01:02:46,554
He chickened out.

802
01:02:47,263 --> 01:02:48,181
Oh, come on.

803
01:02:49,766 --> 01:02:50,600
Sit down.

804
01:02:51,142 --> 01:02:51,976
I'm sorry.

805
01:02:57,190 --> 01:02:59,442
Okay… then, let's start…

806
01:02:59,525 --> 01:03:02,612
from page a hundred and thirty
nine of the textbook today.

807
01:03:07,366 --> 01:03:09,452
"Choi Jeong- yo."

808
01:03:11,120 --> 01:03:11,954
How much?

809
01:03:14,081 --> 01:03:16,042
How much did you donate to get in here?

810
01:03:16,959 --> 01:03:18,920
Pianos? How many?

811
01:03:19,003 --> 01:03:20,838
Two? Three?

812
01:03:20,922 --> 01:03:22,507
Why aren't you saying anything?

813
01:03:23,049 --> 01:03:24,759
- Oh…
- Hey.

814
01:03:25,384 --> 01:03:27,386
Keep this shit up and you'll regret it,

815
01:03:27,470 --> 01:03:28,304
- 'kay?
- Eek.

816
01:03:28,387 --> 01:03:29,222
I'm so scared.

817
01:03:32,934 --> 01:03:35,978
Wow, did they pick you up off the
street? Huh?

818
01:03:37,480 --> 01:03:40,691
Hey, it's cos of low-class kids like him
that our school's reputation is

819
01:03:40,775 --> 01:03:42,235
going down the drain.

820
01:03:42,318 --> 01:03:45,488
I mean, this one - doesn't have
the musical talent to be here.

821
01:03:46,155 --> 01:03:47,782
Not to mention, his background.

822
01:03:49,158 --> 01:03:49,992
Move.

823
01:03:52,495 --> 01:03:55,164
- What's that?
- Can you move? I need my book.

824
01:03:56,290 --> 01:03:57,333
I don't want to.

825
01:03:59,210 --> 01:04:00,169
Hey, hey, hey!

826
01:04:00,795 --> 01:04:01,629
What's going on?

827
01:04:02,421 --> 01:04:03,256
Ya little punks.

828
01:04:03,881 --> 01:04:06,008
- This ain't over…
- Get back to your seats.

829
01:04:07,301 --> 01:04:08,135
Tool…

830
01:04:20,648 --> 01:04:21,607
Thanks for earlier.

831
01:04:22,108 --> 01:04:24,861
- For what?
- You stopped them for me.

832
01:04:26,571 --> 01:04:27,738
I wasn't stopping them.

833
01:04:28,239 --> 01:04:29,699
I just wanted to get my book.

834
01:04:30,616 --> 01:04:33,619
Oh, so that's where you sign up
to use the practice room?

835
01:04:33,703 --> 01:04:35,204
Where can I buy snacks?

836
01:04:35,705 --> 01:04:37,456
You're not in the dorms, right?

837
01:04:37,540 --> 01:04:39,792
Why are arts high schools so damn
complicated?

838
01:04:39,876 --> 01:04:41,919
There are so many weird classes,
don't you think?

839
01:04:42,003 --> 01:04:43,379
All right, that's enough.

840
01:04:46,257 --> 01:04:47,091
What is?

841
01:04:47,174 --> 01:04:49,635
I'm not really big on making friends with
anyone.

842
01:04:50,761 --> 01:04:51,971
You're on your own, man.

843
01:05:50,404 --> 01:05:52,823
Hey, do you have an extra handkerchief?

844
01:06:26,148 --> 01:06:27,525
And the grand prize goes to

845
01:06:27,608 --> 01:06:28,609
Choi Jeong-yo!

846
01:06:29,110 --> 01:06:30,027
Congrats!

847
01:06:31,654 --> 01:06:33,406
Are you out of your mind?

848
01:06:33,489 --> 01:06:35,533
Second place? THAT'S NOT GOOD ENOUGH!

849
01:07:09,984 --> 01:07:11,777
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

850
01:07:12,278 --> 01:07:14,196
Do you seriously not remember me?

851
01:07:14,280 --> 01:07:15,322
Actually,

852
01:07:15,865 --> 01:07:17,491
there's something I haven't told you.

853
01:07:17,575 --> 01:07:18,617
Go study abroad.

854
01:07:18,701 --> 01:07:20,828
Do you really think I'd run off
to go study overseas?!

855
01:07:20,911 --> 01:07:22,663
How about you do a four-hand piece?

856
01:07:23,539 --> 01:07:24,707
You know, Choi Jeong-yo, right?

857
01:07:24,790 --> 01:07:26,751
Let's see. Can't you afford to buy real
sheet music?

858
01:07:26,834 --> 01:07:28,544
- Boom!
- NO DON'T!

859
01:07:28,627 --> 01:07:30,004
- Dammit!
- Why does it have to be with him?

860
01:07:30,087 --> 01:07:31,505
Have you ever heard him play?

861
01:07:31,589 --> 01:07:34,592
I hate jerks who approach music with
an attitude like yours.

862
01:07:35,176 --> 01:07:37,928
I'm afraid Jeong-yo will have to be held
responsible.

863
01:07:38,012 --> 01:07:39,638
So… I'll have to expel him.
